<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <!-- Assembly name is the invoked command, so help usage and the MCP server name read "slnmap". -->
    <AssemblyName>slnmap</AssemblyName>
    <Description>Slnmap (sln-map) — a semantic map of your .sln for AI coding agents. Analyze a .NET solution into a queryable code graph, serve it over MCP, and inspect index status.</Description>
    <PackAsTool>true</PackAsTool>
    <ToolCommandName>slnmap</ToolCommandName>
    <PackageId>Slnmap</PackageId>
    <Version>0.13.1</Version>
    <RollForward>Major</RollForward>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 the Slnmap authors. All rights reserved.</Copyright>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://slnmap.dev</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageTags>dotnet;roslyn;mcp;ai;code-analysis;claude-code;knowledge-graph</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Fix: the cross-stack linker never tried a base-path-stripped fallback for
absolute-URL call sites, so a backend that mounts its controllers without the conventional /api
prefix linked 0/22 real call sites even though the identical dev build linked 22/22 against a
synthetic endpoint set. Now also tries the call site's path with the configured --base-path prefix
stripped from its front, but only as a sequential fallback -- never preferred over an as-authored
match. Any inferred link is visibly marked (via prefix-stripped path) everywhere results are
shown; both candidates matching is disclosed as an ambiguity rather than silently preferred.

Fix: controller-action extraction silently skipped real ASP.NET Core "POCO controllers" -- a
controller with no ControllerBase inheritance at all, discovered by name/attribute convention
instead. Widened via a cheap syntactic prefilter plus a semantic check mirroring ASP.NET's own
convention, measured against a real ~4000-class solution to confirm zero added false-positive
risk. A class that looks controller-ish but still fails the semantic check is now disclosed
(a new ControllerLikeClassesUnrecognized category), never silently invisible.

Added: a disclosed honesty warning when MvcOptions.Conventions.Add(...) registers an
IApplicationModelConvention -- route templates can be mutated at runtime in a way static analysis
can't see, and slnmap does not interpret convention implementations.

Verified end to end against the real gothinkster RealWorld pair: 22/22 call sites linked, all 22
carrying the prefix-stripped/host marker.

Source: https://github.com/EMahmoudNabil/slnmap</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources\viz-template.html" LogicalName="viz-template.html" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Resources\vis-network.min.js" LogicalName="vis-network.min.js" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Slnmap.Analysis\Slnmap.Analysis.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Slnmap.Core\Slnmap.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Slnmap.Mcp\Slnmap.Mcp.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Slnmap.Storage\Slnmap.Storage.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="System.CommandLine" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Slnmap.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
